<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Import / Copy Tracks From Another Field" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormCopyTracks`
    (FormCopyTracks.cs + FormCopyTracks.Designer.cs + FormCopyTracks.resx). The operator picks a
    SOURCE field on the left (only fields that have both Field.txt and TrackLines.txt, excluding the
    current field), the dialog lists that field's tracks on the right, the operator multi-selects one
    or more tracks and imports (copies) them into the currently-open field. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a
    faithful re-platform of the currently rendered Windows Forms surface — never a redesign: no new
    colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind FormCopyTracksView.axaml.cs owns ALL behaviour:
      * Code-behind dialog: NO x:DataType, NO DataContext, NO {Binding} / MVVM. Every control is
        addressed imperatively by its x:Name, exactly like the sibling code-behind dialogs
        (FormFieldDirView / FormSaveOrNotView / FormFilePickerView). The x:Names below are the
        integration contract and MUST stay byte-identical to the originals:
            lbFields  lvTracks  lblStatus
            btnSelectAllTracks  btnDeselectAllTracks  btnCopyToCurrentField  btnClose
      * Event handlers keep the ORIGINAL WinForms method names so the code-behind is a faithful port
        (mirrors FormSaveOrNotView, which kept btnOk_Click etc.): the field-selection handler
        lbFields_SelectedIndexChanged loads the chosen field's tracks; btnSelectAllTracks_Click /
        btnDeselectAllTracks_Click select/clear the track list; btnCopyToCurrentField_Click performs
        the copy; btnClose_Click closes. In WinForms the event WIRING lived in the Designer (which
        this .axaml replaces); the handler bodies live in the .cs (which the .axaml.cs replaces).
      * lvTracks is MULTI-select. This deliberately REPLACES the WinForms per-item colour-toggle
        (lvTracks_MouseClick flipping BackColor between white and green #009600) with a real
        multi-selection list — so there is NO lvTracks click handler; btnCopyToCurrentField_Click
        reads lvTracks.SelectedItems directly. The green selection accent is preserved as a style.
      * Window initialisation (the WinForms FormCopyTracks_Load that populated the field list) is
        owned by the code-behind (constructor / OnOpened), so no Loaded handler is declared here.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormCopyTracks.Designer.cs:
      Text "Import Tracks From Another Field"  -> Title="Import Tracks" (per the assigned file spec;
                                                  the code-behind may localise via gStr at runtime).
      ClientSize 1000 x 700                    -> Width / Height (fixed, matching the WinForms client).
      FormBorderStyle.Fixed3D + ControlBox=false -> CanResize="False": a fixed, bordered dialog. The
                                                  spec does NOT request a borderless shell, so the
                                                  standard window chrome / Title bar is kept (unlike
                                                  the borderless sibling dialogs).
      ShowInTaskbar=false                      -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition.CenterScreen (shown modally over FormGPS) -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
      BackColor Gainsboro / panel1 LightGray   -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}": the
                                                  neutral chrome is themed to the App.axaml day/night
                                                  palette rather than hard-coding a WinForms colour.
      Font Tahoma                              -> FontFamily="Tahoma". WinForms points are converted to
                                                  Avalonia device-independent pixels (pt x 96/72):
                                                  14.25->19 (headers), 16->21 (lists), 11.25->15
                                                  (status), 10->13 (button captions).

    A responsive Grid (NOT an absolute Canvas) reproduces the layout: because the standard Title bar
    is kept, it consumes height, so absolute WinForms coordinates would not line up — the Grid lets the
    two lists fill the available height while preserving the original two-column proportions.

    Colours: the window chrome and all caption / status text use App.axaml's {DynamicResource}
    day/night brushes (AogFrameBrush / AogTextBrush) so the live Light<->Dark switch is observed. The
    two lists keep their distinctive fixed WinForms input backgrounds (lbFields WhiteSmoke, lvTracks
    AliceBlue) with an explicit dark item foreground so the rows stay readable in BOTH themes (the
    WinForms lists were never day/night themed). No WinForms / System.Drawing / OpenTK / GMap
    namespaces are referenced — Avalonia 11.3 markup only. Button glyphs are served from the GPS
    assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs, mapped from the Designer's Resources
    images: SelectAll / DeselectAll / FileNew (Import) / OK64 (Close).
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormCopyTracksView"
        Title="Import Tracks"
        Width="1000"
        Height="700"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <Window.Styles>
        <!-- Flat, chrome-less image+caption buttons: reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
             FlatAppearance.BorderSize=0 + BackColor=Transparent carried by every button in
             FormCopyTracks.Designer.cs. The :pointerover / :pressed / :disabled template overrides
             suppress the Fluent hover / press / disabled fill so only the glyph + caption show — the
             same technique used by the sibling FormFieldDirView / FormSaveOrNotView. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Touch-friendly list rows. The WinForms lists forced a 40px row height via an ImageList
             hack; reproduce it with MinHeight, full-width content (FullRowSelect) and a small indent. -->
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lbFields ListBoxItem">
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="40" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,4" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lvTracks ListBoxItem">
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="40" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,4" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Row text colour is forced DARK on the fixed light list backgrounds so unselected rows stay
             readable in BOTH day and night themes. This is set on the item's ContentPresenter
             (PART_ContentPresenter) rather than the item's inherited Foreground, because the Fluent
             ListBoxItem ControlTheme assigns the presenter foreground DIRECTLY per visual state; a
             directly-set presenter value beats an inherited item value, so an item-level Foreground
             setter never reaches the rendered text. A Window-style presenter setter outranks the
             ControlTheme, so this is the level that actually wins. -->
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lbFields ListBoxItem /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lvTracks ListBoxItem /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
        </Style>

        <!-- lbFields selected row: WinForms highlighted the chosen field DarkOrange (255,140,0) with
             WHITE text (lbFields_SelectedIndexChanged). Reproduced as a selection-triggered style
             (NOT per-item colour code) per the file spec. Both background AND foreground are set on the
             presenter so they override the Fluent selected-state theme values; the :selected:pointerover
             variant keeps the colours while hovering a selected row. -->
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lbFields ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFFF8C00" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="White" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lbFields ListBoxItem:selected:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFFF8C00" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="White" />
        </Style>

        <!-- lvTracks selected rows: WinForms marked selected tracks green #009600 (0,150,0) with WHITE
             text. With multi-select this becomes the standard selection highlight, themed to that
             accent for parity. -->
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lvTracks ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FF009600" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="White" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="ListBox#lvTracks ListBoxItem:selected:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FF009600" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="White" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!-- Outer 5px frame reproduces the WinForms Padding(5) / panel1 inset. Three bands: column headers
         (Auto), the two lists (fill the remaining height), and the status + command-button bar (Auto). -->
    <Grid Margin="5" RowDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">

        <!-- ===================== Row 0 — column headers ===================== -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="*,15,*" Margin="6,2,6,4">
            <!-- lblFieldsHeader: WinForms Label "Available Fields", Tahoma 14.25 Bold (-> 19). -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblFieldsHeader"
                       Grid.Column="0"
                       Text="Available Fields"
                       FontSize="19"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
            <!-- lblTracksHeader: WinForms Label "Available Tracks", Tahoma 14.25 Bold (-> 19). -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblTracksHeader"
                       Grid.Column="2"
                       Text="Available Tracks"
                       FontSize="19"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- ===================== Row 1 — the two lists ===================== -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="1" ColumnDefinitions="*,15,*" Margin="6,0,6,0">

            <!-- lbFields: SOURCE field list. WinForms ListView(Details), BackColor WhiteSmoke,
                 Tahoma 16 Regular (-> 21), single-select. Avalonia ListBox, SelectionMode="Single".
                 SelectionChanged loads the selected field's tracks (lbFields_SelectedIndexChanged).
                 Field-name items are supplied by the code-behind; no ItemTemplate / bindings. -->
            <ListBox x:Name="lbFields"
                     Grid.Column="0"
                     SelectionMode="Single"
                     Background="#FFF5F5F5"
                     BorderBrush="#FFB0B8C0"
                     BorderThickness="1"
                     FontSize="21"
                     ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                     SelectionChanged="lbFields_SelectedIndexChanged" />

            <!-- lvTracks: tracks available in the selected field, each shown as
                 "<name> (AB Line|Curve|<mode>)" (built by the code-behind). WinForms ListView(Details),
                 BackColor AliceBlue, Tahoma 16 Bold (-> 21). MULTI-select replaces the WinForms colour
                 toggle. Selected rows use the green accent style above. No selection handler — the copy
                 button reads SelectedItems directly. -->
            <ListBox x:Name="lvTracks"
                     Grid.Column="2"
                     SelectionMode="Multiple"
                     Background="#FFF0F8FF"
                     BorderBrush="#FFB0B8C0"
                     BorderThickness="1"
                     FontSize="21"
                     FontWeight="Bold"
                     ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- ================= Row 2 — status line + command buttons ================= -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="2" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="6,6,6,2">

            <!-- lblStatus: bottom-left status line (WinForms Label, Tahoma 11.25 -> 15). The default
                 text is the Designer placeholder; the code-behind overwrites it at runtime
                 ("Found N field(s) with tracks", progress messages, errors). -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="lblStatus"
                       Grid.Column="0"
                       Text="Select a field from the left, then select tracks to copy"
                       FontSize="15"
                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />

            <!-- Command buttons, right-aligned. Two visual groups mirror the WinForms spacing:
                 {Select All, Deselect All} then a gap then {Import, Close}. Each is a 100 x 90 flat
                 image-above-caption button (WinForms TextImageRelation.ImageAboveText). Native glyphs
                 are 64 x 64; shown at 48 x 48 (Uniform) per the sibling convention. -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="32"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                        VerticalAlignment="Bottom">

                <!-- group A: select / deselect all tracks -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <!-- btnSelectAllTracks: image SelectAll, caption "Select All". -->
                    <Button x:Name="btnSelectAllTracks"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="100" Height="90"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Select All"
                            Click="btnSelectAllTracks_Click">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SelectAll.png"
                                   Width="48" Height="48" Stretch="Uniform" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Select All" FontSize="13" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Button>
                    <!-- btnDeselectAllTracks: image DeselectAll, caption "Deselect All". -->
                    <Button x:Name="btnDeselectAllTracks"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="100" Height="90"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Deselect All"
                            Click="btnDeselectAllTracks_Click">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/DeselectAll.png"
                                   Width="48" Height="48" Stretch="Uniform" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Deselect All" FontSize="13" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- group B: import (copy) / close -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10">
                    <!-- btnCopyToCurrentField: the copy / import action. WinForms image FileNew,
                         caption "Import". Reads lvTracks.SelectedItems and copies them to the
                         current field (btnCopyToCurrentField_Click). -->
                    <Button x:Name="btnCopyToCurrentField"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="100" Height="90"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Import"
                            Click="btnCopyToCurrentField_Click">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/FileNew.png"
                                   Width="48" Height="48" Stretch="Uniform" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Import" FontSize="13" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Button>
                    <!-- btnClose: closes the dialog (btnClose_Click). WinForms image OK64,
                         caption "Close". -->
                    <Button x:Name="btnClose"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="100" Height="90"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Close"
                            Click="btnClose_Click">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="2"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                                   Width="48" Height="48" Stretch="Uniform" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Close" FontSize="13" FontWeight="Bold"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>

            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
